@baseUrl = http://localhost:5080

# =============================================================
#  Logging with Serilog: Console, Text file and Azure Blob
#  Start the API (F5), send each request, then watch the logs.
# =============================================================

### LG1. Log in (Information: "User ... logged in")
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "sara.ahmed@example.com",
  "password": "Clinic2026!"
}

### LG2. Register a patient (Information: "Patient ... registered")
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/patients
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": "Imran",
  "lastName": "Qureshi",
  "dateOfBirth": "1987-09-03",
  "gender": "Male",
  "maritalStatus": "Married",
  "nationalityCode": "IN",
  "identityType": "Passport",
  "identityNumber": "P{{$randomInt 1000000 9999999}}",
  "mobileNumber": "+9198{{$randomInt 10000000 99999999}}",
  "address": { "line1": "5 Charminar Road", "city": "Hyderabad" }
}

### LG3. Wrong password (Warning: "Login failed")
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "sara.ahmed@example.com",
  "password": "WrongPassword1"
}

### LG4. Something breaks (Error, with the full exception)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/diagnostics/error
